{
 "id": "thm-weil-pbc-bounded-below",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Bounded-below derived proper base change",
 "statement": "For a cartesian square [def-weil-pbc-cartesian-square] with $f$ proper and\nevery $K\\in\\Dplus(X_{\\Et})$ with torsion cohomology,\n\n$$\n \\Ex_{\\square,K}:g^{-1}Rf_*K\n \\xrightarrow{\\sim}Rf'_*g'^{-1}K\n$$\n\nis an isomorphism in $\\Dplus(Y'_{\\Et})$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-properbasechange/thm-weil-pbc-bounded-below.md",
  "place": "node thm-weil-pbc-bounded-below, order 1320"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-pbc-cartesian-square",
  "def-weil-pbc-derived-categories",
  "def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The exchange morphism of [def-weil-pbc-derived-exchange] induces the morphism\nof hypercohomology spectral sequences whose $E_2$ map is the exchange map for\nthe torsion cohomology sheaf $\\mathcal H^q(K)$, an isomorphism by\n[lemma-weil-pbc-torsion-assembly]; the differential compatibility is\n[lem-weil-pbc-exact-couple-differential]. If $\\mathcal H^q(K)=0$ for $q<a$,\nthen in fixed total degree $n$ only $a\\leq q\\leq n$ occurs by\n[lemma-weil-pbc-hypercohomology-convergence], so both filtrations are finite,\nexhaustive, and separated. Page induction gives an isomorphism on $E_\\infty$,\nand induction on the finite filtration gives an isomorphism on each abutment;\nthe abutment identification [lemma-weil-pbc-exact-couple-abutment] identifies\nthat abutment map with the cohomology map of the named mate, which is\ntherefore an isomorphism.",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-pbc-derived-exchange",
    "lemma-weil-pbc-torsion-assembly",
    "lem-weil-pbc-exact-couple-differential",
    "lemma-weil-pbc-hypercohomology-convergence",
    "lemma-weil-pbc-exact-couple-abutment"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
